# HKDSE 英文寫作實用句式 (Useful Phrases for HKDSE English Writing)

## 1. 引言/開頭 (Introduction)

### 背景/現況 (Background/Current Situation)
- In recent years, there has been growing concern about...
- Nowadays, it is widely acknowledged that...
- In today's society, ... has become a hot topic
- The issue of... has attracted much attention
- It is a common phenomenon that...
- In contemporary society, there is mounting apprehension regarding...
- The contemporary discourse surrounding... has garnered unprecedented attention
- The prevailing zeitgeist is characterised by increasing preoccupation with...
- This issue has assumed paramount significance in the public consciousness
- There has been a paradigm shift in how society perceives...

### 提出話題 (Introducing the Topic)
- When it comes to..., people's opinions vary
- The topic of... has sparked heated debate
- There is no denying that... is a controversial issue
- ... is a matter of great concern to many people
- The question of whether... has been widely discussed
- The contentious nature of... has engendered polarised perspectives
- This multifaceted issue has precipitated extensive scholarly and public discourse
- The debate surrounding... has become increasingly polarised
- This subject matter has generated considerable intellectual ferment
- The discourse on... has evolved into a complex tapestry of competing viewpoints

### 表明立場 (Stating Your Position)
- From my perspective,...
- I firmly believe that...
- In my opinion,...
- It is my view that...
- I am convinced that...
- I am of the firm conviction that...
- It is my considered opinion that...
- I subscribe to the view that...
- I am firmly persuaded that...
- My position is predicated on the belief that...
- I maintain an unwavering stance that...

### 引用數據/統計 (Quoting Data/Statistics)
- According to recent statistics,...
- Research shows that...
- Studies have revealed that...
- Data indicates that...
- Statistics demonstrate that...
- A survey conducted by... found that...
- Empirical evidence suggests that...
- Statistical analysis reveals a compelling correlation between...
- Scholarly research has consistently demonstrated that...
- Quantitative analysis substantiates the contention that...
- The empirical data points unequivocally to the conclusion that...
- Longitudinal studies have yielded compelling evidence that...

### 引用例子/故事 (Quoting Examples/Stories)
- Take... as an example
- A case in point is...
- Consider the case of...
- For instance,...
- To illustrate this point,...
- A pertinent illustration would be...
- This phenomenon is epitomised by the case of...
- A paradigmatic example serves to illuminate this point:...
- The case of... serves as a compelling exemplar of...
- Historical precedent demonstrates that...

---

## 2. 利弊分析 (Pros and Cons)

### 優點/好處 (Advantages/Benefits)
- One of the main advantages is that...
- The most significant benefit is...
- It is beneficial to... because...
- ... brings about numerous benefits, such as...
- A major merit of... is that...
- One cannot overlook the manifold advantages, most notably...
- The preponderance of benefits, including..., renders this proposition highly compelling
- The advantages are multifarious and far-reaching
- This approach yields a plethora of positive outcomes
- The intrinsic merits of this proposition are manifold
- The benefits accrue across multiple dimensions

### 缺點/壞處 (Disadvantages/Drawbacks)
- However, there are also drawbacks to consider
- On the negative side,...
- One major disadvantage is...
- The downside of... is that...
- ... may lead to several problems, including...
- Conversely, one must acknowledge the inherent limitations, particularly...
- Notwithstanding its merits, this approach is not without its concomitant drawbacks
- The potential pitfalls are not to be dismissed lightly
- This proposition is fraught with inherent risks
- The disadvantages, though not immediately apparent, are nonetheless significant
- One must exercise caution regarding the potential adverse ramifications

### 平衡觀點 (Balanced View)
- While there are benefits, we must also consider...
- Despite the advantages, we cannot ignore...
- It is important to weigh both sides of the argument
- We need to strike a balance between... and...
- Taking everything into account,...
- A nuanced analysis necessitates a comprehensive evaluation of both the merits and demerits
- The optimal approach lies in achieving an equilibrium between competing considerations
- A judicious assessment requires careful consideration of both perspectives
- The most prudent course of action entails synthesising the competing viewpoints
- One must navigate the delicate balance between... and...

---

## 3. 論證/同意/不同意 (Argue/Agree/Disagree)

### 同意 (Agreement)
- I completely agree with the view that...
- I am in full agreement with...
- There is no doubt that...
- I share the same opinion that...
- I strongly support the idea that...
- I wholeheartedly endorse the proposition that...
- I find myself in unequivocal alignment with the contention that...
- I am in complete accord with the assertion that...
- My position is entirely congruent with the view that...
- I unreservedly subscribe to the notion that...

### 不同意 (Disagreement)
- I strongly disagree with the statement that...
- I cannot accept the view that...
- It is my firm belief that this is not the case
- I am opposed to the idea that...
- I take issue with the claim that...
- I find this assertion fundamentally flawed and untenable
- This proposition is, in my estimation, fundamentally misconceived
- I must respectfully but firmly dissent from this viewpoint
- This argument is predicated on a series of erroneous assumptions
- I find myself compelled to challenge the validity of this contention

### 部分同意 (Partial Agreement)
- While I agree that..., I cannot accept that...
- I partially agree, but...
- To some extent, I agree, however...
- Although there is some truth in this,...
- I see your point, but...
- While I concede that..., I must nevertheless maintain that...
- Whilst there is merit in the argument that..., I would contend that...
- I acknowledge the validity of certain aspects, yet I must demur regarding...
- There is a kernel of truth in this, but it fails to account for...
- While I am sympathetic to the view that..., I cannot fully endorse...

### 提出論據 (Presenting Arguments)
- First and foremost,...
- Another compelling argument is that...
- Furthermore, it should be noted that...
- Moreover,...
- In addition,...
- A further cogent consideration is that...
- It is also pertinent to observe that...
- An additional line of reasoning suggests that...
- One must also take into account the fact that...
- The argument gains further credence when one considers that...

### 反駁 (Refuting)
- However, this argument fails to consider...
- Critics may argue that..., but...
- While some may claim that..., the reality is...
- This view overlooks the fact that...
- Contrary to popular belief,...
- This line of reasoning is rendered invalid by the fact that...
- Such an argument is predicated on a fundamental misapprehension
- This contention collapses under closer scrutiny
- The flaw in this reasoning becomes apparent when one examines...
- This argument is undermined by the following considerations:...

---

## 4. 給予建議 (Giving Advice)

### 建議/提議 (Suggestions/Recommendations)
- I would strongly recommend that...
- It would be advisable to...
- My suggestion is to...
- I propose that...
- You might want to consider...
- I would urge you to consider...
- It would be prudent to contemplate...
- I would counsel you to...
- It would be judicious to...
- My counsel would be to...

### 應該/必須 (Should/Must)
- It is essential that...
- It is crucial to...
- You should definitely...
- It is imperative that...
- One must...
- It is of paramount importance that...
- One cannot overstate the necessity of...
- It is incumbent upon one to...
- There is an imperative need to...
- The exigency of this matter demands that...

### 避免/不要 (Avoiding)
- You should avoid...
- It is not advisable to...
- Steer clear of...
- Refrain from...
- Do not...
- It would be ill-advised to...
- One would be well-advised to eschew...
- Prudence dictates that one should abstain from...
- It would be counterproductive to...
- One should exercise caution in...

### 如果...就... (If...then...)
- If you..., you will...
- Should you..., you can...
- In the event that..., you should...
- Provided that..., you will...
- In the eventuality that..., it would be expedient to...
- Were you to..., the likely outcome would be...
- In the hypothetical scenario where..., one would be well-served to...

---

## 5. 建議/提議 (Suggestions)

### 提出建議 (Making Suggestions)
- I would like to suggest that...
- It is my recommendation that...
- I propose the following measures:
- One possible solution would be to...
- I put forward the idea that...
- I would advocate for the implementation of...
- It is my considered recommendation that...
- I would submit that the following course of action be adopted:...
- My proposal entails the following strategic initiatives:...
- I would posit that the optimal approach would be to...

### 列舉建議 (Listing Suggestions)
- First of all, we should...
- Secondly, it is important to...
- Additionally,...
- Last but not least,...
- Furthermore, it is imperative that...
- In addition, one cannot overemphasise the significance of...
- A further critical consideration is that...
- It is also incumbent upon us to...
- Another pivotal measure would be to...

### 強調重要性 (Emphasizing Importance)
- It is of utmost importance that...
- We cannot stress enough the need to...
- Particular attention should be paid to...
- Special consideration must be given to...
- It is incumbent upon us to recognise the criticality of...
- The significance of this matter cannot be overstated
- This warrants the highest priority
- The gravity of this situation demands immediate attention
- This is a matter of the highest import

---

## 6. 報告 (Reports)

### 報告開頭 (Report Opening)
- The purpose of this report is to...
- This report aims to investigate/examine...
- The following report presents findings on...
- I have been asked to report on...
- This report endeavours to elucidate...
- The present report seeks to provide a comprehensive analysis of...
- This document constitutes a thorough investigation into...
- The ensuing report offers an in-depth examination of...

### 描述發現 (Describing Findings)
- The investigation revealed that...
- It was found that...
- The survey results indicate that...
- According to the data collected,...
- The evidence suggests that...
- The findings point to the conclusion that...
- The empirical data substantiates the hypothesis that...
- The research yields compelling evidence that...
- The data provides unequivocal support for the proposition that...
- The investigation has brought to light the following significant findings:...

### 描述方法/過程 (Describing Methods/Processes)
- The research was conducted by...
- Data was collected through...
- The investigation involved...
- The following methodology was used:...
- The process consisted of...
- The research methodology employed a multi-faceted approach, encompassing...
- Data acquisition was facilitated through a combination of...
- The investigative process entailed a systematic approach involving...
- A rigorous methodological framework was adopted, comprising...

### 分析數據/趨勢 (Analyzing Data/Trends)
- The figures show a significant increase in...
- There has been a dramatic rise in...
- The data reveals a downward trend in...
- A comparison of the statistics indicates...
- The pattern suggests that...
- Statistical analysis reveals a pronounced upward trajectory in...
- The data exhibits a discernible pattern, indicative of...
- The statistical evidence points to a clear correlation between...
- A comprehensive analysis of the data reveals a compelling trend:...
- The metrics demonstrate a consistent pattern of...

### 結論 (Conclusion)
- In conclusion,...
- To sum up,...
- Based on the findings, it can be concluded that...
- The report concludes that...
- In light of the evidence presented, one may reasonably infer that...
- The cumulative findings point unequivocally to the conclusion that...
- The weight of evidence compels us to conclude that...
- The preponderance of evidence supports the following conclusion:...

### 建議行動 (Recommending Action)
- It is recommended that...
- I would suggest that immediate action be taken to...
- Steps should be taken to...
- Measures need to be implemented to...
- It is imperative that remedial measures be expeditiously implemented
- The situation warrants the immediate adoption of comprehensive strategies
- Urgent intervention is required to address...
- The gravity of the situation necessitates the following measures:...

---

## 7. 提案 (Proposals)

### 提出提案 (Presenting Proposals)
- I am writing to propose that...
- I would like to put forward a proposal for...
- The following proposal outlines...
- This proposal aims to...
- I wish to submit a proposal concerning...
- I respectfully submit the following proposal for your consideration
- I would like to present a comprehensive proposal regarding...
- The following represents a detailed proposal for...

### 說明理由 (Explaining Reasons)
- The reason for this proposal is...
- This is necessary because...
- The rationale behind this is...
- This proposal addresses the need to...
- The impetus for this proposal stems from...
- This proposal is predicated on the recognition that...
- The underlying rationale for this initiative is...
- This proposal is motivated by the imperative to...

### 預期效果 (Expected Outcomes)
- This would result in...
- The expected benefits include...
- It is anticipated that...
- This is likely to lead to...
- The envisaged outcomes encompass a range of positive developments, including...
- It is projected that this initiative will engender...
- The anticipated ramifications include...
- This is expected to yield the following benefits:...

### 請求批准 (Requesting Approval)
- I hope you will consider this proposal favourably
- I would appreciate your support for this proposal
- I look forward to your approval
- Your consideration of this matter would be greatly appreciated
- I would be most grateful for your favourable consideration of this proposal
- Your endorsement of this initiative would be instrumental in its success
- I trust that you will recognise the merit of this proposal
- Your support would be invaluable in bringing this initiative to fruition

---

## 8. 投訴信 (Complaints)

### 投訴開頭 (Complaint Opening)
- I am writing to express my dissatisfaction with...
- I wish to complain about...
- I am writing to bring to your attention...
- I feel compelled to write regarding...
- I am writing to register my profound dissatisfaction with...
- I am writing to lodge a formal complaint regarding...
- I find it necessary to bring to your attention a matter of grave concern:...

### 描述問題 (Describing Problems)
- The main issue is that...
- I encountered the following problems:
- What concerns me most is...
- I was disappointed to find that...
- The primary grievance pertains to...
- The most egregious aspect of this matter is...
- The crux of my complaint centres on...
- I was dismayed to discover that...

### 表達不滿 (Expressing Disappointment)
- I was extremely disappointed with...
- I found it unacceptable that...
- This is completely unsatisfactory
- I am appalled by...
- I find this state of affairs utterly deplorable
- This represents a flagrant breach of acceptable standards
- This falls far short of the standards one would reasonably expect
- The level of service rendered was woefully inadequate

### 要求行動 (Requesting Action)
- I demand that immediate action be taken
- I expect you to...
- I would appreciate it if you could...
- I hope you will take appropriate measures to...
- I look forward to your prompt response
- I trust that you will expedite the resolution of this matter
- I would expect nothing less than immediate and comprehensive remedial action
- I require a prompt and satisfactory resolution to this matter
- I trust that you will address this issue with the urgency it warrants

### 威脅後果 (Threatening Consequences)
- Unless this matter is resolved, I will be forced to...
- If no action is taken, I will have no choice but to...
- I reserve the right to take further action if...
- In the absence of a satisfactory resolution, I shall have no alternative but to...
- Should this matter remain unresolved, I will be constrained to pursue all available avenues of redress
- Failing a prompt resolution, I will be obliged to escalate this matter
- In the event that this issue is not addressed satisfactorily, I will have recourse to...

---

## 9. 演講 (Speeches)

### 開場白 (Opening)
- Good morning/afternoon, ladies and gentlemen
- I am honoured to be here today to speak about...
- Thank you for giving me this opportunity to...
- It gives me great pleasure to address you on the topic of...
- It is both a privilege and an honour to address this distinguished gathering
- I am deeply gratified to have the opportunity to speak before such an esteemed audience
- It is with great humility that I stand before you today to discuss...

### 吸引注意 (Gaining Attention)
- Have you ever wondered...?
- Imagine if...
- Let me begin with a question:...
- I would like to start by asking you...
- Permit me to pose a thought-provoking question:...
- I invite you to contemplate the following:...
- Allow me to present a scenario that may challenge your preconceptions:...

### 過渡 (Transitions)
- Moving on to my next point,...
- Let me now turn to...
- Another important aspect is...
- Furthermore,...
- Having established this, I would now like to address...
- This naturally leads us to consider...
- Building upon this foundation, I would now like to explore...
- This brings me to my next consideration:...

### 強調重點 (Emphasizing Points)
- I cannot stress enough that...
- What I want to emphasize is...
- The key point here is...
- Most importantly,...
- It is imperative that we recognise the fundamental importance of...
- The crux of the matter lies in...
- The pivotal consideration is that...
- This point cannot be overstated:...

### 呼籲行動 (Calling for Action)
- I urge you to...
- Let us work together to...
- It is time for us to...
- I call upon all of you to...
- I implore each and every one of you to...
- I would exhort you to take decisive action in...
- I beseech you to join me in this endeavour
- The time has come for us to collectively commit to...

### 結尾 (Closing)
- In conclusion, I would like to say that...
- To wrap up,...
- Thank you for your attention
- I hope my speech has given you food for thought
- I trust that my remarks have provided you with ample material for reflection
- I trust that the perspectives I have shared will resonate with you and inspire meaningful action
- May the ideas I have presented today serve as a catalyst for positive change
- I leave you with this thought:...

---

## 10. 連接詞/轉折詞 (Connectives/Transitions)

### 順序 (Sequence)
- 首先 (First) - First, Firstly, First of all, To begin with, Initially, Primarily, In the first instance, In the first place, To commence, At the outset, First and foremost, In the initial stages
- 其次 (Second) - Second, Secondly, Next, Then, Subsequently, Thereafter, In the second place, Following this, In the next instance, Sequentially, In succession, In turn
- 最後 (Finally) - Finally, Lastly, Last but not least, In conclusion, Ultimately, In the final analysis, To conclude, To culminate, In the final reckoning, In the ultimate analysis, As a final point, To bring matters to a close

### 遞進 (Addition)
- 而且 (Moreover) - Moreover, Furthermore, In addition, Additionally, What's more, What is more, Equally importantly, By the same token, In the same vein, Similarly, Correspondingly, In like manner, Analogously, In a similar fashion, Complementarily, Augmenting this point
- 另外 (Besides) - Besides, Also, As well as, Not only...but also, In conjunction with, Coupled with, Together with, Alongside, In tandem with, In parallel with, Complemented by, Supplemented by, In concert with

### 對比 (Contrast)
- 但是 (But) - But, However, Nevertheless, Nonetheless, Yet, Notwithstanding, Be that as it may, Having said that, That said, All the same, Even so, Still, In spite of this, For all that, At the same time, On the flip side
- 雖然 (Although) - Although, Though, Even though, Despite, In spite of, Notwithstanding the fact that, Albeit, Albeit that, While, Whilst, Whereas, Much as, Granted that, Admitting that, For all that
- 相反 (On the contrary) - On the contrary, Conversely, In contrast, On the other hand, Contrariwise, In contradistinction, By contrast, As opposed to, In opposition to, Inversely, Per contra, On the flip side, In reverse, Diametrically opposed

### 原因 (Cause)
- 因為 (Because) - Because, Since, As, Due to, Owing to, By virtue of, As a consequence of, On account of, In view of, In light of, Given that, Seeing that, Inasmuch as, For the reason that, On the grounds that, Attributable to, Stemming from, Arising from
- 所以 (Therefore) - Therefore, Hence, Thus, As a result, Consequently, Ergo, Accordingly, It follows that, For this reason, As a consequence, In consequence, Wherefore, For that reason, This being the case, In that case, Under these circumstances

### 舉例 (Examples)
- 例如 (For example) - For example, For instance, Such as, Like, To cite an instance, To exemplify, A case in point, To illustrate, By way of illustration, As an illustration, To demonstrate, To show, As evidence, To cite a case, As a demonstration, In exemplification, To adduce an example
- 具體來說 (Specifically) - Specifically, In particular, To illustrate, To elucidate, Namely, That is to say, To be precise, To be exact, In specific terms, More precisely, More specifically, In detail, In particular detail, To particularise, To specify

### 總結 (Summary)
- 總括來說 (In summary) - In summary, To sum up, In conclusion, To conclude, All in all, To recapitulate, In summation, In essence, In brief, In short, To summarise, In a nutshell, To encapsulate, In the final analysis, In the main, On the whole, By and large, In the aggregate, Taken together, Collectively speaking

### 條件 (Condition)
- 如果 (If) - If, Provided that, As long as, On condition that, In case, Subject to, Contingent upon, Assuming that, Supposing that, Given that, In the event that, Should, Were...to, In the circumstance that, On the assumption that, With the proviso that, Conditional upon
- 除非 (Unless) - Unless, If not, Otherwise, Failing which, In the absence of, Barring, Save for, Except if, But for, Without, Lacking, In default of, In want of

### 讓步 (Concession)
- 即使 (Even if) - Even if, Even though, Although, Though, Albeit, Notwithstanding, Granted that, Admitting that, Allowing that, While, Whilst, Much as, For all that, Despite the fact that, In spite of the fact that, Regardless of the fact that
- 儘管 (Despite) - Despite, In spite of, Regardless of, Irrespective of, Notwithstanding, In defiance of, In the face of, Undeterred by, Unmindful of, Heedless of, Unheeding of, In contempt of

### 目的 (Purpose)
- 為了 (In order to) - In order to, So as to, For the purpose of, With the aim of, With a view to, With the intention of, With the objective of, With the goal of, For the sake of, To the end that, So that, With a mind to, In the interest of, With the design of
- 以免 (Lest) - Lest, So that...not, In case, For fear that, To avoid, To prevent, To avert, To forestall, To obviate, To preclude, To stave off, To ward off

### 時間 (Time)
- 當...時 (When) - When, While, As, During, Throughout, In the course of, Whilst, At the time when, At the moment that, In the period when, Concurrently with, Coincident with, Synchronously with, Simultaneously with
- 之後 (After) - After, Following, Subsequently, Afterwards, In the wake of, In the aftermath of, Subsequent to, Following on from, In the sequel, Thereafter, Later, Later on, In due course, In the fullness of time, Post, Following which
- 之前 (Before) - Before, Prior to, Previously, Antecedent to, Preceding, Earlier, Earlier on, In advance of, Ahead of, Pre-, Ante-, Foregoing, Preceding which, Prior to which
- 同時 (Meanwhile) - Meanwhile, At the same time, Simultaneously, Concurrently, In parallel, Coincidentally, Synchronously, In tandem, At once, All at once, In unison, In concert, In synchrony, In parallel with, At the same moment

### 強調 (Emphasis)
- 確實 (Indeed) - Indeed, In fact, Actually, As a matter of fact, Veritably, In truth, Truly, Really, Genuinely, Undoubtedly, Unquestionably, Indisputably, Unarguably, In reality, In actuality, In point of fact, As it happens, In effect
- 特別 (Especially) - Especially, Particularly, Specifically, Notably, Predominantly, Above all, Chiefly, Primarily, Mainly, Principally, In particular, Most notably, Most importantly, Significantly, Markedly, Remarkably, Strikingly, Conspicuously

### 限定 (Limitation)
- 然而 (However) - However, Nevertheless, Nonetheless, Still, Yet, Be that as it may, Having said that, That said, All the same, Even so, In spite of this, For all that, At the same time, On the other hand, But then again, On the flip side, Conversely, In contrast
- 不過 (But) - But, However, Yet, Still, On the other hand, Nevertheless, Nonetheless, All the same, Even so, That said, Having said that

### 補充說明 (Clarification)
- 換句話說 (In other words) - In other words, That is to say, To put it differently, To rephrase, To put it another way, To express it differently, To state it otherwise, To phrase it differently, To articulate it differently, To formulate it differently, To couch it differently
- 即是 (That is) - That is, Namely, i.e., Viz., To wit, That is to say, In other words, Specifically, In particular, To be specific, To be precise, More precisely, More specifically

---

## 11. 申請信 (Application Letters)

### 申請開頭 (Application Opening)
- I am writing to apply for the position of...
- I wish to apply for... as advertised in...
- I am writing in response to your advertisement for...
- I would like to express my interest in...
- I am writing to submit my application for the position of...
- I am writing to express my keen interest in the aforementioned position
- I am writing to formally submit my candidacy for...
- I wish to tender my application for the position of...

### 說明資格/經驗 (Stating Qualifications/Experience)
- I hold a... degree in... from...
- I have... years of experience in...
- My background in... makes me well-suited for...
- I am currently working as... at...
- I have completed internships at...
- My extensive experience in... has equipped me with...
- My academic credentials, coupled with my professional experience in..., render me eminently qualified for...
- My professional trajectory has been characterised by...
- I have amassed considerable expertise in...
- My track record demonstrates consistent excellence in...

### 表達興趣/動機 (Expressing Interest/Motivation)
- I am particularly interested in... because...
- I am drawn to this opportunity because...
- What appeals to me most is...
- I am excited about the prospect of...
- This position aligns perfectly with my career goals
- This opportunity resonates deeply with my professional aspirations and values
- The prospect of contributing to... is particularly compelling
- This role represents an ideal convergence of my skills and interests

### 說明能力/技能 (Stating Abilities/Skills)
- I am proficient in...
- I possess strong skills in...
- My strengths include...
- I have demonstrated my ability to...
- I am confident in my ability to...
- My track record demonstrates a consistent ability to...
- I have consistently excelled in...
- I have a proven capacity for...
- My expertise encompasses...
- I have demonstrated exceptional competency in...

### 結尾請求 (Closing Request)
- I would welcome the opportunity to discuss my application further
- I look forward to hearing from you
- I would be grateful for an interview
- I hope you will consider my application favourably
- Thank you for considering my application
- I would be most appreciative of the opportunity to discuss how my qualifications align with your requirements
- I would be delighted to elaborate on any aspect of my application
- I trust that my credentials will merit your favourable consideration

---

## 12. 描述趨勢/變化 (Describing Trends/Changes)

### 上升/增加 (Increase/Rise)
- There has been a significant increase in...
- ... has risen dramatically
- The number of... has grown substantially
- ... shows an upward trend
- ... has experienced a sharp rise
- A steady increase can be observed in...
- The data evinces a pronounced upward trajectory in...
- A marked escalation has been discernible in...
- The statistics reveal a substantial uptick in...
- There has been a notable surge in...
- The figures demonstrate a progressive upward movement

### 下降/減少 (Decrease/Decline)
- There has been a marked decrease in...
- ... has dropped considerably
- The figure for... has fallen sharply
- ... shows a downward trend
- ... has witnessed a significant decline
- A gradual decrease can be seen in...
- The statistics reveal a precipitous decline in...
- A discernible downward spiral is evident in...
- The data points to a substantial downturn in...
- There has been a notable contraction in...
- The metrics indicate a progressive diminution

### 穩定/持平 (Stable/Steady)
- ... has remained stable
- The level of... has stayed constant
- ... shows little change
- There has been no significant change in...
- ... has plateaued at...
- The figures have exhibited remarkable stability, hovering around...
- A state of relative equilibrium has been maintained
- The data reveals a period of sustained stability
- The trend has remained relatively static
- There has been minimal fluctuation in...

